# Build context for wildgrove-cms/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads this file instead of the context root's .dockerignore when the
# build names that Dockerfile with -f, which is why each app carries its own.
#
# Two things matter here. Keeping the context small: node_modules and .next are
# gigabytes that the build regenerates anyway. And keeping secrets out: an
# environment file that reached the context could be copied into a layer and
# shipped inside the published image.

# ── Never, under any circumstances ───────────────────────────────
# The negations come last on purpose: a later pattern overrides an earlier one,
# so `.env.example` survives the two rules above it.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# ── Regenerated by the build ─────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
**/dist
packages/db/generated
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# ── Not needed to build or run ───────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
**/.gitignore
.github
wildgrove-vault
scripts
compose.yaml
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.dockerignore
README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# ── Local tooling ────────────────────────────────────────────────
.claude
.codex
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
